#
# Clean conformance fixture for math:ConditionedAssertionShape (Rule P8): a
# math:ConditionalProbability P(A | B) that names its conditioning context through
# math:conditionalOn — the B — as a measure-theoretic math:ProbabilityEvent (not typed
# logic:Event, so P11 stays satisfied on it). It MUST raise NO probability failure class.
# Positive counterpart of counter-examples/conditional-probability-unconditioned.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConditionalProbabilityConditioned).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:posteriorProbability a math:ConditionalProbability ;
    math:conditionalOn ex:evidenceEvent .

ex:evidenceEvent a math:ProbabilityEvent .
